geo.append({'key':'AU','stance':stance('^AXJO'),'label':'financing relief / household test','parts':sourceparts([
('Macro Stance',r'Reserve Bank of Australia|\bRBA\b|Australia.*(?:rate|inflation)','australia',None,"Australia's rate-sensitive allocation depends on whether financing relief improves household spending without restarting price pressure. Mortgage cash flow can respond before businesses commit to hiring or investment, so the initial equity benefit may be narrower than a broad cyclical rally implies. Prefer companies with repeat demand and disciplined capital spending over those relying on a rapid housing or discretionary spending acceleration. The external channel remains separate: commodity and export revenues can move for reasons unrelated to domestic household purchasing power. Keep the policy trade and the export trade distinct when choosing the instrument."),
('Demand & Financing',r'Australia.*(?:job|employment|wage|consumer|econom)|Australian.*(?:job|wage|consumer)','australia','monthly',"The useful confirmation is an improvement in real cash flow alongside employment stability. A household that saves its financing relief behaves differently from one that increases discretionary purchases, and retailers' margins will reveal that distinction before a broad economic label does. Bank earnings require attention to credit quality and deposit competition as well as loan volumes. For foreign investors, the currency can amplify or dilute the local equity result. Demand improvement that comes with disciplined lending would support domestic exposure more convincingly than a short-lived bounce driven by the next policy headline."),
('Playbook ✓',r'Australia.*(?:stocks|shares)|Australian.*(?:stocks|shares)|ASX|\bRBA\b','australia',None,"Hold selective domestic franchises and add housing-sensitive exposure only when financing relief becomes completed activity rather than enquiries. Keep resource positions tied to their own supply, cost and demand evidence. The risk is a policy disappointment arriving while household confidence remains fragile; that would favour defensive cash generation over operating leverage. A convincing pickup in spending with stable credit quality would justify widening the allocation. Use currency hedging where the thesis is domestic earnings rather than a deliberate view on global risk appetite.")])})
