geo.append({'key':'PL','stance':stance('EPOL'),'label':'easing opportunity / fiscal discipline','parts':sourceparts([
('Macro Stance',r'NBP|RPP|Poland.*(?:inflation|rate|GDP)|Polsc.*(?:inflac|stóp|PKB)|inflacja|polski.*PKB','poland_pl','monthly',"Poland's domestic opportunity should be judged through real incomes, the cost of credit and the persistence of inflation. Households can benefit from softer price pressure, but a durable consumption recovery also needs confidence in employment and disposable income. For companies, cheaper credit helps most when it accompanies viable investment rather than simply refinancing an existing burden. The equity implication is selective exposure to domestic activity with pricing power and manageable leverage. Banks, retailers and infrastructure suppliers share a sensitivity to policy, but the effect on their margins and balance sheets is different. Keep those distinctions explicit before calling the whole market a rate-cut trade."),
('Markets',r'WIG20|GPW|złot|zloty|Poland.*(?:stocks|bond)|polskich.*(?:obligac|akcji)','poland_pl',None,"The Warsaw allocation combines local earnings, the currency and the global willingness to own emerging European risk. A foreign investor can be right about company profits and still lose through currency translation, while a domestic investor sees a different opportunity cost. Prefer earnings-supported leadership over a rally driven entirely by changes in discount rates. Banks deserve scrutiny for funding costs, loan quality and distributions; retailers need volume growth that does not sacrifice profitability. State-linked energy and utility companies require attention to investment commitments and policy objectives as well as near-term valuation. Keep the expression specific enough that the position can be reviewed when one of those channels changes."),
('Fiscal & Politics',r'Poland.*(?:budget|deficit|president|Nawrocki)|budżet|deficyt|Nawrocki|prezydent','poland_pl',None,"Fiscal choices affect Poland through bond supply, household income and the credibility of medium-term financing. A supportive spending programme can lift selected orders while also increasing the risk premium attached to long-duration assets. Political disagreement matters most when it changes implementation or the predictability of taxes and regulation, rather than when it merely adds another headline. Companies with a clear operating catalyst should not be valued as though every public commitment will immediately become revenue. The stronger investment case comes from funded contracts, identifiable beneficiaries and execution capacity. Keep fiscal support separate from a claim that the sovereign financing constraint has disappeared."),
('Corporate & Sectors',r'Orlen|PKO|PZU|KGHM|JSW|Dino|Allegro|CD Projekt|LPP|PGE|mBank','poland_pl',None,"Company selection matters because the local macro tailwind can be offset by sector-specific costs. For lenders, policy easing can stimulate demand but also change interest margins. For power and energy businesses, cash generation has to be considered alongside capital expenditure and regulatory obligations. Retailers need evidence that improving purchasing power becomes profitable sales, while commodity producers remain exposed to product prices and their own operating costs. Gaming and technology franchises should be valued on delivery and cash generation rather than a national growth label. The portfolio should therefore contain explicit earnings theses, each with a trigger that can be checked independently of the broad Warsaw index."),
('Geopolitics & Security',r'Poland.*(?:Ukraine|Russia|NATO|defen)|Polska.*(?:Ukrain|Rosj|NATO|obron)|Ukrain|Rosj|NATO|obron','poland_pl',None,"Security spending can create long-lived demand, but investors need to distinguish announced commitments from procurement, production capacity and profitable delivery. The geopolitical premium can also affect the currency and sovereign financing cost, which means the national equity story carries both an industrial opportunity and a risk overlay. Avoid assuming that every listed defence-adjacent business captures the same economics. Orders without the ability to execute can create working-capital pressure rather than immediate shareholder returns. A more stable regional risk environment would help financing, while renewed uncertainty would favour stronger balance sheets and measured position sizes rather than a blanket retreat from domestic companies."),
('New / Most Important',r'Poland.*(?:growth|consumer|industry)|PKB|produkcj|sprzedaż|wynagrodzen|bezroboci','poland_pl','monthly',"The main test is whether the domestic recovery broadens from income relief into investment and profitable private demand. A better activity reading should be compared with wages, employment and corporate margins before it supports a lasting rerating. Foreign capital can amplify the move once the operating evidence improves, but that potential flow is a scenario rather than a substitute for earnings. Watch for companies able to convert local demand into free cash flow without stretching working capital. If inflation stabilises while activity strengthens, the investment case becomes less dependent on the next policy decision and more attractive to investors seeking durable domestic exposure."),
('Playbook ✓',r'Poland.*(?:econom|stocks)|WIG|GPW|polsk.*gospodark|NBP|RPP','poland_pl',None,"Own selected domestic compounders and lenders where valuation, capital strength and earnings delivery agree. Add cyclical exposure as improving sales and investment confirm the real-income recovery; reduce it if financing costs or fiscal uncertainty rise faster than expected cash generation. Keep regulated energy exposure sized to the credibility of its investment and distribution framework. Currency risk deserves its own budget for foreign investors rather than being buried inside the equity allocation. ⚠ Divergence: domestic growth optimism can coexist with a demanding fiscal and geopolitical risk premium, so a rising local index does not remove the need to monitor bonds, the currency and company cash conversion.")])})
